00:12:19,928 --> 00:12:21,761
-(Yuji yelling)
-(thudding)

260
00:12:21,845 --> 00:12:23,012
[Announcer] Home run!

261
00:12:23,094 --> 00:12:25,887
-(thudding)
-(Yuji groaning)

262
00:12:25,971 --> 00:12:28,387
Should you really be revealing

263
00:12:28,470 --> 00:12:30,014
something like
that to the enemy?

264
00:12:30,138 --> 00:12:32,430
It's no problem to reveal
a technique like that

265
00:12:32,513 --> 00:12:33,430
to an opponent.

266
00:12:33,513 --> 00:12:35,639
In fact, it can even
work to your advantage--

267
00:12:35,723 --> 00:12:37,431
I want to focus on the curse,

268
00:12:37,514 --> 00:12:40,473
but it feels like I should
be listening to him.

269
00:12:40,557 --> 00:12:41,974
There is merit to it.

270
00:12:42,057 --> 00:12:44,224
Revealing one's hand
is a gambling tactic

271
00:12:44,308 --> 00:12:47,099
that increases the
effectiveness of one's technique.

272
00:12:47,182 --> 00:12:48,433
I'll show you.

273
00:12:48,516 --> 00:12:51,392
(puddle splashing)

274
00:12:53,059 --> 00:12:56,143
(creature murmuring)

275
00:12:59,894 --> 00:13:02,811
(explosion blasting)

276
00:13:02,894 --> 00:13:04,520
(blood sploshing)

277
00:13:04,603 --> 00:13:07,270
(creature murmuring)

278
00:13:07,353 --> 00:13:08,937
(blood sploshing)

279
00:13:09,021 --> 00:13:12,771
(blood dripping)

280
00:13:13,187 --> 00:13:15,023
(blood splashing)

281
00:13:15,105 --> 00:13:16,939
All of that force came from me.

282
00:13:18,397 --> 00:13:19,857
Oh man.

283
00:13:19,940 --> 00:13:22,106
Not only is the blade he
used completely wrapped,

284
00:13:22,189 --> 00:13:22,982
but he used the back of it

285
00:13:23,065 --> 00:13:25,649
to slice right
through that thing.

286
00:13:26,941 --> 00:13:29,025
Behind you, Itadori.

287
00:13:30,233 --> 00:13:31,317
Huh?

288
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:34,233
-(creature growling)
-(thudding)

289
00:13:34,567 --> 00:13:35,609
(Yuji groaning)

290
00:13:35,693 --> 00:13:37,044
I don't like you turning
your back on your opponent.

291
00:13:37,068 --> 00:13:39,861
You're the one who
keeps distracting me here!

292
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:42,986
(creature growling)

293
00:13:48,070 --> 00:13:50,988
(energy billowing)

294
00:13:55,238 --> 00:13:59,280
[Satoru] Your cursed energy
comes up a little slow, huh?

295
00:14:00,448 --> 00:14:01,156
So, what's that mean?

296
00:14:01,239 --> 00:14:03,531
Your cursed energy can't keep up

297
00:14:03,614 --> 00:14:05,699
with your explosive power.

298
00:14:05,782 --> 00:14:08,198
You're still not good at
collecting your cursed energy,

299
00:14:08,282 --> 00:14:09,907
so it lags behind.

300
00:14:09,991 --> 00:14:13,408
But in effect, that creates
an irregular energy flow.

301
00:14:14,616 --> 00:14:16,534
The moment after
your fist impacts,

302
00:14:16,617 --> 00:14:17,993
your cursed energy slams in,

303
00:14:18,076 --> 00:14:21,036
so you're creating two
impacts with every stroke.

304
00:14:21,118 --> 00:14:24,160
(Yuji groaning)

305
00:14:24,243 --> 00:14:26,619
(thudding)

306
00:14:28,037 --> 00:14:31,829
(blood sploshing)

307
00:14:38,663 --> 00:14:40,873
Divergent fist.

308
00:14:40,956 --> 00:14:41,956
So sick!

309
00:14:43,040 --> 00:14:45,247
It's not a skill many
sorcerers have.

310
00:14:46,041 --> 00:14:47,957
This weapon will serve you well.

311
00:14:48,707 --> 00:14:49,749
Hm.

312
00:14:50,165 --> 00:14:53,374
[Kento] Is his
raw strength superhuman?

313
00:14:53,458 --> 00:14:56,250
His initial blow has very
little cursed energy to it,

314
00:14:56,334 --> 00:15:00,417
but it reaches 120% of an
average sorcerer's power.

315
00:15:00,500 --> 00:15:02,261
Then the real blow of
cursed energy flows in.

316
00:15:04,501 --> 00:15:06,586
It must be unimaginably
unpleasant for

317
00:15:06,669 --> 00:15:07,210
those struck by it.

318
00:15:07,294 --> 00:15:09,045
He has room to grow too.

319
00:15:09,127 --> 00:15:13,378
If he can learn to imbue
100% of his cursed energy

320
00:15:13,462 --> 00:15:16,128
into 100% of his martial arts,

321
00:15:16,211 --> 00:15:18,921
now I see why Gojo
brought him to me.

322
00:15:19,338 --> 00:15:21,422
Mm?

323
00:15:21,505 --> 00:15:23,380
Oh, pardon me, I'll end you now.

324
00:15:24,172 --> 00:15:27,923
(intense ambient music)

325
00:15:28,007 --> 00:15:28,465
Itadori, wait.

326
00:15:28,548 --> 00:15:30,298
Don't finish it off yet.

327
00:15:32,716 --> 00:15:33,716
Have a look at this.

328
00:15:35,382 --> 00:15:37,633
It's a picture I took
of my opponent.

329
00:15:37,717 --> 00:15:40,717
But I thought curses didn't
show up in photographs?

330
00:15:41,550 --> 00:15:43,593
Please listen to me calmly.

331
00:15:45,010 --> 00:15:46,650
These creatures that
we've been fighting--

332
00:15:49,719 --> 00:15:51,094
They're human.

333
00:15:51,177 --> 00:15:54,470
Well, I guess I ought to
call them former humans.

334
00:15:54,553 --> 00:15:57,096
They're similar to the
three from the theater.

335
00:15:57,179 --> 00:15:58,429
The structure of their bodies

336
00:15:58,512 --> 00:16:00,262
was forcibly altered
by a curse technique.

337
00:16:00,346 --> 00:16:02,114
If that was all, I would
have noticed from the start.

338
00:16:02,138 --> 00:16:05,347
The two we just fought
were more than just altered.

339
00:16:05,430 --> 00:16:08,181
They were full of cursed
energy like cursed spirits are.

340
00:16:08,264 --> 00:16:09,765
You'll have to ask the culprit

341
00:16:09,848 --> 00:16:12,474
to explain his curse
technique to you.

342
00:16:12,557 --> 00:16:13,849
Though there is evidence

343
00:16:13,932 --> 00:16:15,199
their brain stems have
been tampered with,

344
00:16:15,223 --> 00:16:19,892
most likely to create confusion
and impaired consciousness.

345
00:16:19,975 --> 00:16:21,516
If they can tamper
with the brain,

346
00:16:21,600 --> 00:16:23,726
it might be possible for
them to modify someone

347
00:16:23,809 --> 00:16:25,684
to be able to use cursed energy.

348
00:16:25,768 --> 00:16:26,601
The relationship
between the brain

349
00:16:26,684 --> 00:16:29,435
and cursed energy is
still a black box to us.

350
00:16:30,769 --> 00:16:32,310
Oh wait, is Itadori listening?

351
00:16:32,393 --> 00:16:34,394
Yeah, I'm here.

352
00:16:35,811 --> 00:16:38,104
I think it's important
you understand this much.

353
00:16:38,187 --> 00:16:39,687
These guys died from the shock

354
00:16:39,771 --> 00:16:41,729
of what happened
to their bodies,

355
00:16:41,812 --> 00:16:43,188
so you didn't kill them.

356
00:16:43,271 --> 00:16:46,563
Don't get the wrong
idea about that.

357
00:16:46,646 --> 00:16:47,688
Thanks.

358
00:16:51,606 --> 00:16:52,731
That's easy to say.

359
00:16:52,815 --> 00:16:56,024
The weight of those two
deaths still feels pretty heavy.

360
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:59,108
Whatever this
thing is we're after,

361
00:17:00,025 --> 00:17:01,900
it disgusts me to the core.

362
00:17:03,650 --> 00:17:05,585
[Kento] This
boy can get sincerely angry

363
00:17:05,609 --> 00:17:07,026
on behalf of others.

364
00:17:08,360 --> 00:17:10,568
Most likely, those
residuals were a bluff

365
00:17:10,651 --> 00:17:12,193
left purposely to lure us in.

366
00:17:12,276 --> 00:17:14,235
Our foe is quite skilled.

367
00:17:14,319 --> 00:17:18,570
It looks like this will take
more than moderate effort,

368
00:17:18,653 --> 00:17:20,112
so let's go all out.

369
00:17:21,112 --> 00:17:22,779
(Yuji chuckling)

370
00:17:22,862 --> 00:17:23,905
Yeah.

371
00:17:25,863 --> 00:17:27,571
There are cursed spirits

372
00:17:27,654 --> 00:17:31,155
known as special grade
potential apparitions.

373
00:17:31,238 --> 00:17:33,073
Cursed spirits are a collection

374
00:17:33,155 --> 00:17:35,365
of the cursed energy
emitted by humans.

375
00:17:35,448 --> 00:17:36,948
Whether it exists or not,

376
00:17:37,032 --> 00:17:39,574
a shared image of
fear makes it easy

377
00:17:39,657 --> 00:17:43,449
for a powerful
curse to manifest.

378
00:17:43,532 --> 00:17:46,158
So, what's an example
of a shared image of fear?

379
00:17:46,241 --> 00:17:49,284
You mean like monsters
and scary ghost stories?

380
00:17:49,368 --> 00:17:51,618
Yes.

381
00:17:51,701 --> 00:17:55,410
Like Toilet-Bound Hanako,
the Nine-Tailed Fox, and so on.

382
00:17:55,494 --> 00:17:56,619
Jujutsu Sorcerers label them

383
00:17:56,702 --> 00:17:58,786
special grade
potential apparitions

384
00:17:58,870 --> 00:18:00,286
and keep watch for them.

385
00:18:00,370 --> 00:18:03,578
And the fact that
they often categorize

386
00:18:03,661 --> 00:18:06,329
powerful unidentified
curses as potential apparitions,

387
00:18:06,412 --> 00:18:09,997
it makes it feel like that's
all they're focused on.

388
00:18:11,205 --> 00:18:13,288
But people constantly
fear other things too,

389
00:18:13,372 --> 00:18:15,289
not just those old fairytales.

390
00:18:16,748 --> 00:18:18,289
Like earthquakes?

391
00:18:18,373 --> 00:18:19,999
(Mahito chuckling)

392
00:18:20,083 --> 00:18:22,707
I love how stress free
it can be talking to you.

393
00:18:23,916 --> 00:18:26,291
Well, I don't really...

394
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:29,501
(creatures growling)

395
00:18:31,376 --> 00:18:32,376
Huh?

396
00:18:34,460 --> 00:18:39,502
People, the ocean,
the forests, the earth,

397
00:18:39,586 --> 00:18:41,503
they fear all of them.

398
00:18:42,961 --> 00:18:45,295
Because the cursed energy
directed towards those

399
00:18:45,379 --> 00:18:46,379
is far too vast,

400
00:18:46,462 --> 00:18:49,713
they gained wisdom
before they took shape

401
00:18:49,797 --> 00:18:52,047
and they've remained
in hiding up until now.

402
00:18:53,630 --> 00:18:56,547
I'm proud to call all
of them my friends.

403
00:18:58,756 --> 00:19:00,256
Tell me, Mahito,

404
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:02,256
what kind of a curse are you?

405
00:19:04,799 --> 00:19:05,800
Human.

406
00:19:06,925 --> 00:19:10,509
I'm a curse that was born
from the hatred and fear

407
00:19:10,592 --> 00:19:13,342
that people hold deep
inside toward others.

408
00:19:13,425 --> 00:19:16,468
(creatures growling)

409
00:19:18,802 --> 00:19:20,445
I've organized the reports
concerning recent residuals,

410
00:19:20,469 --> 00:19:23,552
unnatural deaths,
and disappearances.

411
00:19:24,969 --> 00:19:27,929
This should narrow down the
culprits hideout to some extent.

412
00:19:28,012 --> 00:19:29,762
Oh yeah, are we storming in?

413
00:19:29,845 --> 00:19:31,554
No. As I said, it's
only to some extent.

414
00:19:31,638 --> 00:19:34,596
While I continue
investigating this matter,

415
00:19:34,679 --> 00:19:36,806
I'd like you to handle
a different task.

416
00:19:37,806 --> 00:19:39,931
This is the boy who
was at the theater,

417
00:19:40,014 --> 00:19:40,556
Junpei Yoshino.

418
00:19:40,640 --> 00:19:41,765
We've just determined

419
00:19:41,848 --> 00:19:44,515
that he goes to the same
high school as the three victims.

420
00:19:46,599 --> 00:19:48,100
Based on his actions

421
00:19:48,182 --> 00:19:50,557
and the way he carries himself
in the surveillance footage,

422
00:19:50,641 --> 00:19:52,522
I believe it's unlikely
that he is a curse user.

423
00:19:54,475 --> 00:19:56,935
However, if he's related
to the victims in some way,

424
00:19:57,018 --> 00:19:58,476
that changes things.

425
00:19:58,559 --> 00:19:59,976
Curse user?

426
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:03,103
Our term for an
evil Jujutsu Sorcerer.

427
00:20:03,185 --> 00:20:05,560
I've entrusted the
process to Iguchi here

428
00:20:05,644 --> 00:20:08,937
and I'd like the two of you
to investigate Junpei together.

429
00:20:09,020 --> 00:20:10,020
Sure.

430
00:20:10,062 --> 00:20:11,270
Come to think of it,

431
00:20:11,354 --> 00:20:13,813
you're the only assistant
we have as far as I know.

432
00:20:13,896 --> 00:20:16,438
Well, I am the only
one of the assistants

433
00:20:16,522 --> 00:20:18,271
who knows that
you're still alive.

434
00:20:18,355 --> 00:20:19,355
So, here I am.

435
00:20:19,438 --> 00:20:22,065
All right, that makes sense.

436
00:20:22,148 --> 00:20:23,148
Let's go!

437
00:20:23,689 --> 00:20:27,524
(footsteps pattering)

438
00:20:29,066 --> 00:20:31,983
You don't just know the
location to some extent, do you?

439
00:20:32,067 --> 00:20:34,191
You know it exactly.

440
00:20:34,274 --> 00:20:36,150
Of course. If the
culprit had wanted to,

441
00:20:36,233 --> 00:20:37,442
he could have left the scene

442
00:20:37,526 --> 00:20:39,651
without leaving behind
any residuals at all.

443
00:20:40,734 --> 00:20:42,944
It would seem we're
being lured in once again.

444
00:20:44,610 --> 00:20:45,669
Weighing the risk
of storming in alone

445
00:20:45,693 --> 00:20:48,361
versus taking Itadori along,

446
00:20:48,444 --> 00:20:50,986
I simply made the safest choice.

447
00:20:51,070 --> 00:20:53,404
He is after all still a child.

448
00:20:54,113 --> 00:20:55,029
-(Iguchi groaning)
-Oh!

449
00:20:55,113 --> 00:20:56,404
And hey, teacher?

450
00:20:56,487 --> 00:20:58,072
Itadori!

451
00:20:58,155 --> 00:20:59,696
Forgot to tell ya,

452
00:20:59,780 --> 00:21:00,780
you be careful.

453
00:21:03,322 --> 00:21:07,698
Itadori, I'm not a teacher
so please don't call me that.

454
00:21:07,782 --> 00:21:08,698
[Yuji] So, Kento dude!

455
00:21:08,782 --> 00:21:10,323
[Kento] I will slap you.

456
00:21:12,158 --> 00:21:14,491
(suspenseful ambient music)

457
00:21:14,574 --> 00:21:15,574
[Iguchi] There he is.

458
00:21:15,616 --> 00:21:17,992
[Yuji] Huh, where's his uniform?

459
00:21:18,076 --> 00:21:18,700
It looks like he hasn't been

460
00:21:18,784 --> 00:21:20,534
attending school for some time.

461
00:21:23,284 --> 00:21:25,576
(stoplight beeping)

462
00:21:25,660 --> 00:21:27,160
We'll get out and
walk from here.

463
00:21:30,285 --> 00:21:31,327
Let's go.

464
00:21:37,203 --> 00:21:39,913
-(people chattering)
-(suspenseful music)

465
00:21:39,996 --> 00:21:43,039
(creature murmuring)

466
00:21:45,789 --> 00:21:48,790
(Closing Theme Music)

467
00:23:15,890 --> 00:23:18,223
-(whimsical music)
-Juju Stroll.

468
00:23:18,306 --> 00:23:19,349
Hey, Nanami.

469
00:23:19,433 --> 00:23:20,641
Let's go out.

470
00:23:20,724 --> 00:23:22,391
No, thank you.

471
00:23:22,474 --> 00:23:23,391
No, seriously,

472
00:23:23,474 --> 00:23:25,350
I have something
to talk to you about.

473
00:23:25,434 --> 00:23:25,976
[Kento] Oh, that is awful.

474
00:23:26,059 --> 00:23:28,350
I didn't say anything yet.

475
00:23:28,434 --> 00:23:29,476
Hm.

476
00:23:29,560 --> 00:23:31,768
(elegant piano music)

477
00:23:38,519 --> 00:23:39,562
Hm?

478
00:23:42,104 --> 00:23:43,603
(intense ambient music)

479
00:23:43,687 --> 00:23:44,729
Mm.

480
00:23:44,813 --> 00:23:49,188
(intense orchestral music)

